{#
  How an association or a person is written out in a link.

  Under laminas this is Schoenstatt\View\Helper\FormatAssociation and
  FormatPerson, reached through SionModel's `formatEntity` dispatcher. None of the
  three can be called from here: each ends in `$this->view->url()`, which wants a
  RouteMatch off the MvcEvent a Symfony-served route does not have. So the
  *decisions* those helpers make are reproduced here — with their defaults, in their
  order, producing their markup — against laminas_path() instead.

  Defaults taken from FormatAssociation::__invoke() with no options, which is how
  both shrine tables call it: display=name, so showFlag, displayAsLink and
  editPencil are all on and showLabel is off.
#}

{#
  The deleted branch is FormatAssociation's own first branch, and it has to come before
  anything touches the record.

  When a change log row names an entity that no longer exists, SionTable substitutes a
  placeholder — `{isDeleted: true, associationId: N, associationName: 'Association Id: N'}`
  and nothing else. `FormatAssociation::__invoke()` opens by testing `isDeleted` and, if
  set, takes the name from `associationName` and turns the link, the label and the pencil
  off; the flag never arises because it lives in the display-name branch it skipped.

  Reproducing that is not optional here the way an unused option would be. Twig runs with
  `strict_variables`, so `entity.country` on a three-key placeholder does not evaluate to
  null as it would in PHP — it raises, after the response has been assembled, which is the
  fatal-200 wedge: `/en/sm/view-changes` answered **200 with zero bytes**. Recorded 28
  times from 2026-08-12 before anything connected it to a deleted record, because until
  `association-delete` was repaired on 2026-08-14 nothing could delete an association
  through the interface to produce such a row on purpose.
#}
{%- macro association(entity) -%}
    {%- if entity.isDeleted ?? false -%}
        {{- entity.associationName -}}
    {%- else -%}
    {%- set locale = current_locale() -%}
    {%- if entity.country %}{{ flag(entity.country) }}&nbsp;{% endif -%}
    {%- set name = entity.nameByLocale[locale] -%}
    {%- if is_allowed('route/association') -%}
        <a href="{{ laminas_path('association', {'sw_id': entity.identifier, 'slug': entity.slugByLocale[locale]}) }}">{{ name }}</a>
    {%- else -%}
        {{- name -}}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- edit_pencil('association', entity.identifier) -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#
  display=kind, whose defaults are the mirror image: no link, no pencil, no flag
  needed. The label comes from Schoenstatt\Service\AssociationKindsService, which
  has already translated it — hence no translate() here, exactly as the helper
  comments say.
#}
{%- macro association_kind(entity, kind_labels) -%}
    {{- kind_labels[entity.kind] is defined ? kind_labels[entity.kind] : translate(entity.kind) -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#
  FormatPerson::__invoke() with no options: last-name-first, title shown, flag
  shown, linked, edit pencil on, labels off. The leading guard is its guard —
  a person with no name at all renders as nothing rather than as an empty link.

  **`displayEditPencil` is honoured, and it has to be.** This macro took no options
  until 2026-08-13, so the one the application actually passes was silently dropped:
  `_assignments-table.html.twig` defaults it to false — because the row already carries
  the *assignment's* pencil right after the name — and every assignment row on every
  ported association page was rendering both. Measured on /en/SL100001A: laminas emits
  `…persons/81">Catoggio, P. Juan Pablo</a><a href="…assignments/50/edit">`, the ported
  page emitted an extra `<a href="…persons/81/edit">` between the two. Nothing failed;
  the page just quietly offered a link the original does not.

  The other five options FormatPerson reads — nameFormat, showTitle, showFlag, link,
  showLabels — are **deliberately not reproduced**, because no call site in this
  application passes any of them and a branch nothing exercises is a branch nothing
  checks. JUser's `formatPerson($person, ['editPencil' => true])` looks like a sixth and
  is not: the helper reads `displayEditPencil`, so that key has never done anything, and
  JUser is unported besides. Add a branch here the day a caller needs it, not before.
#}
{%- macro person(person, options = {}) -%}
    {#- `?? null` throughout the guard, for the deleted-record placeholder.

        A change log row naming a person who no longer exists carries only
        `{isDeleted, personId, <nameField>}`. FormatPerson has no isDeleted branch of its
        own and does not need one: in PHP the absent `firstName`/`lastName` read as null,
        the guard fails, and the helper renders nothing. That is the behaviour to match.

        Twig runs with `strict_variables`, so reading an absent key raises instead of
        answering null, and the guard that was supposed to reject the placeholder was the
        thing that crashed on it. Same defect the association() macro above carries the
        long note about. -#}
    {%- if (person.personId ?? null) and person.personId != '' and ((person.firstName ?? null) is not null or (person.lastName ?? null) is not null) -%}
        {%- if person.country ?? null %}{{ flag(person.country) }}&nbsp;{% endif -%}
        {%- set first = person.title ? translate(person.title) ~ ' ' ~ person.firstName : person.firstName -%}
        {%- set name = person.lastName ? person.lastName ~ ', ' ~ first : first -%}
        <a href="{{ laminas_path('persons/person', {'person_id': person.personId}) }}">{{ name }}</a>
        {%- if person.deathDate %} (✝{{ person.deathDate|date('Y') }}){% endif -%}
        {%- if options.displayEditPencil ?? true -%}{{- edit_pencil('person', person.personId) -}}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#
  The dispatcher: what `$this->formatEntity($type, $data, $options)` resolves to.

  `formatEntity` is Schoenstatt\View\Helper\FormatEntity, which switches on the entity
  type before deferring to SionModel's general implementation:

      person       -> formatPerson       -> the person() macro above
      association  -> formatAssociation  -> the association() macro above
      role         -> its own inline markup, not reproduced
      publication  -> formatPublication, not reproduced (via SionModel's own deferral)
      everything else -> format_entity(), i.e. App\Laminas\EntityFormatter

  The switch lives here rather than in PHP for one reason: two of its branches are the
  macros in this file, and a Twig function cannot call a macro. `formats_entity_generally()`
  is what keeps the two lists from drifting — it asks EntityFormatter whether it will
  accept the type, so a type added to its SPECIALIZED list without a branch here raises
  instead of being formatted by the wrong rules.
#}
{%- macro entity(entity_type, data, options = {}) -%}
    {%- if entity_type == 'association' -%}
        {#- options are accepted and dropped on purpose: the only one any caller passes
            is `showLabel => false`, which is FormatAssociation's own default under
            display=name, so honouring it and ignoring it produce the same bytes. -#}
        {{- _self.association(data) -}}
    {%- elseif entity_type == 'person' -%}
        {{- _self.person(data, options) -}}
    {%- elseif formats_entity_generally(entity_type) -%}
        {{- format_entity(entity_type, data, options) -}}
    {%- else -%}
        {#- role and publication: laminas formats these with a helper nobody has
            reproduced yet. format_entity() raises a LogicException naming the type,
            which is what should happen — plausible-but-wrong markup on an admin page is
            worse than a loud failure. -#}
        {{- format_entity(entity_type, data, options) -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
